Id: stor003i
Severity: INFO
Category: filesystem
Check: check_storage
References: tmpfs(5)
Controls: CIS 4.1; NIST CM-6; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

/tmp is a directory on the root file system rather than a file system
of its own, so it shares the root's mount options and cannot have
nosuid, nodev and noexec (stor001w, stor002i), and filling it fills
the root file system. Debian 13 and Fedora already mount a tmpfs there.

To fix it, enable the tmpfs systemd ships ('systemctl enable
tmp.mount'; on Ubuntu copy /usr/share/systemd/tmp.mount to
/etc/systemd/system first), or add 'tmpfs /tmp tmpfs
nosuid,nodev,noexec,mode=1777 0 0' to /etc/fstab, and reboot.
